1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:05,696
The brush clears a model of a temple, with a tower curved like a beehive.

2
00:00:05,696 --> 00:00:12,207
Temples in different parts of India have different tower shapes. A trained eye can tell the region from the roof.

3
00:00:12,207 --> 00:00:15,659
How can you tell a temple's region from its roof?

4
00:00:32,883 --> 00:00:41,454
How do we know? The temples survive, and archaeologists dug up the sites around them. Inscriptions name donors and builders.

5
00:00:41,454 --> 00:00:45,216
The Shilpashastras are texts on the art of building.

6
00:01:00,950 --> 00:01:08,276
Indian temples have a common plan. The sanctum is the garbhagriha. In front is a hall, the mandapa.

7
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:16,494
Above the sanctum rises a tower. Three styles are named after the shape of that tower. The Nagara style is found in the north.

8
00:01:16,494 --> 00:01:20,444
Its tower, the shikhara, curves inward like a beehive.

9
00:01:20,444 --> 00:01:28,074
The temples of Khajuraho, and the Sun Temple at Konark in Odisha, are Nagara. The Dravida style is found in the south.

10
00:01:28,074 --> 00:01:36,302
Its tower, the vimana, rises in stepped tiers, and gateways, called gopurams, grow taller in later centuries.

11
00:01:36,302 --> 00:01:43,436
The Pallava temples and the Brihadeeswara temple are Dravida. The Vesara style is a mix, found in the Deccan.

12
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:46,480
It blends Nagara and Dravida features.

13
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:53,472
The Hoysala temples at Belur and Halebidu, with star-shaped plans and very fine carving, are Vesara.

14
00:01:53,472 --> 00:02:00,890
Some scholars use these three terms for convenience, and point out that the old texts use them in various ways.

15
00:02:16,617 --> 00:02:26,855
Old name, new name. The Sun Temple at Konark is in the state once called Orissa. In 2011, the official English name became Odisha.

16
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:32,339
The temple is a World Heritage Site, and a masterpiece of the Nagara style.

17
00:02:48,083 --> 00:02:56,671
Carve this tip into memory. Nagara north: shikhara. Dravida south: vimana. Vesara mix.

18
00:02:56,671 --> 00:03:03,762
North, south and in between, and a tower for each. Name the tower and you know the style.

19
00:03:19,483 --> 00:03:35,390
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. Which style has a curved beehive tower? The answer: Nagara. Number two.

20
00:03:35,390 --> 00:03:46,555
Which style has a stepped tower and tall gateways? The answer: Dravida. Number three.

21
00:03:46,555 --> 00:03:57,909
Which style blends the other two in the Deccan? The answer: Vesara. Now one line for Mains.

22
00:03:57,909 --> 00:04:03,883
Explain the Nagara, Dravida and Vesara styles of temple architecture.

23
00:04:23,617 --> 00:04:33,144
The temple model goes into its case. Its tower tells you where it belongs. Three facts to take away. A model of a temple tower.

24
00:04:33,144 --> 00:04:42,125
Nagara, Dravida and Vesara styles. Sanctum, hall and tower. Next gallery: The Whole Gallery.

